\lispPackageChapter{chorus/api/nvcc}

This package finds \texttt{nvcc} and invokes it.
\texttt{chorus/api} reexports \texttt{*tmp-path*}, \texttt{*nvcc-options*},
\texttt{*nvcc-binary*}, \texttt{find-nvcc}, \texttt{nvcc-available-p}, and
\texttt{nvcc-arch-option}. \texttt{nvcc-compile}, \texttt{find-msvc-cl}, and
\texttt{arch-option-p} stay in this package.

\lispVariableSubsection{*tmp-path*}

Directory for temporary \texttt{.cu} and \texttt{.ptx} files. \texttt{nil}
means \texttt{uiop:temporary-directory}.

\lispVariableSubsection{*nvcc-options*}

Extra command-line options passed to \texttt{nvcc}.

\lispVariableSubsection{*nvcc-binary*}

Path to \texttt{nvcc}. \texttt{nil} or the string \texttt{nvcc} means
auto-detect, using \texttt{PATH}, \texttt{CUDA\_PATH}, and the usual toolkit
locations on Windows and Unix.

\lispFunctionSubsection{nvcc-arch-option}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(nvcc-arch-option \lispVar{major} \lispVar{minor})}

Returns an \texttt{-arch=sm\_XY} option. Compute capability 12.0 becomes
\texttt{sm\_120}. \texttt{major} is a nonnegative integer. \texttt{minor} is
an integer from 0 through 9.

\lispFunctionSubsection{nvcc-available-p}

True when an \texttt{nvcc} binary can be found.

\lispFunctionSubsection{find-nvcc}

Returns the \texttt{nvcc} pathname that auto-detect selected.

\lispFunctionSubsection{find-msvc-cl}

Returns the Windows host compiler \texttt{cl.exe} when one is found.

\lispFunctionSubsection{nvcc-compile}

Compiles a CUDA C string to PTX. The include path passed to \texttt{nvcc} is
the \texttt{include/} directory of the \texttt{chorus} system.

\lispFunctionSubsection{arch-option-p}

True when an option list already contains an architecture selector.
